// Can a full-screen program show the terminal's cursor where the next
// character will go?
//
// Hypothesis DIS-ZYE-004 (HALLAZGOS.md). Today it cannot: `>>|` hides the
// cursor on entry and nothing in the language shows it. This program is what an
// editor does on its first frame: draw a line, then wait for a key with the
// caret after the text. When the finding is decided, the line that shows the
// cursor goes where the comment says, and check.py should report FIXED.
>>| {
    >>!
    >>~ (1, 1) > "hello"
    // here: show the terminal's cursor at row 1, column 6
    <<| _k
}
